WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.435
The four cardinal directions are north, east, south and west; a quarter-turn moves to

00:00:05.435 --> 00:00:06.557
the next direction.

00:00:07.367 --> 00:00:13.170
Face south. Turn a quarter-turn right. Which way now? The answer is west. Use the

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:15.879
compass order N–E–S–W; after turning, face west.

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:21.657
A learner faces south at a market stall and turns half a turn. Which direction is

00:00:21.657 --> 00:00:23.825
faced next? Pause the video and think.

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:30.514
A learner faces south at a market stall and turns half a turn. Which direction is

00:00:30.514 --> 00:00:35.601
faced next? The answer is north. Use the compass order N–E–S–W; after turning, face

00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:35.964
north.
